WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.704
The school week joins obstetrics, neonates, pediatrics and tracheostomy care. Each domain still begins with the same question: what threatens this patient now?
学校周内容连接产科、新生儿、儿科及气切照护；每个领域仍从同一问题开始：当前最威胁患者的是什么？

00:00:10.704 --> 00:00:21.768
The lessons already covered the seven-E special-populations module, birth complications, neonatal transition, APGAR concepts and the assigned tracheostomy topic.
前面课程已讲7E特殊人群模块、分娩并发症、新生儿过渡、APGAR概念及指定气切主题。

00:00:21.768 --> 00:00:32.448
This rehearsal uses different ages and facts from the saved school cases. The values below are invented training data, not patient records or assessment answers.
本演练使用不同于学校保存案例的年龄及细节；下列数值为虚构训练数据，不是真实患者记录或考核答案。

00:00:32.448 --> 00:00:44.568
A narrated class cannot certify birth maneuvers, newborn ventilation, Broselow use or suctioning. Demonstrate each skill on appropriate training equipment under school supervision.
配音课件不能认证分娩手法、新生儿通气、Broselow使用或吸引；每项技能都需在学校监督下用适当训练器材演示。

00:00:44.568 --> 00:00:53.520
At a birth, maternal and newborn needs can overlap. Assign separate attention without allowing either patient’s assessment to disappear.
分娩中母婴需要可能重叠；应分配独立关注，同时不能遗漏任何一方评估。

00:00:53.520 --> 00:01:03.432
Name who leads each patient, who tracks time and who calls for additional resources. Confirm that each request was heard and completed.
需明确母婴各自负责人、计时者及增援联络者，并确认每项请求都已接收完成。

00:01:03.432 --> 00:01:12.024
Coordinate with a registered midwife when present. Their legal professional scope does not automatically transfer to EMS personnel.
有注册助产士在场时应协调；其法定专业范围不会自动转移给EMS人员。

00:01:12.024 --> 00:01:23.232
A partner should interrupt immediately for an airway, breathing, hemorrhage or newborn-ventilation concern. Shared situational awareness outranks a completed checklist.
伙伴发现气道、呼吸、出血或新生儿通气问题时应立即打断；共同态势感知高于完成清单。

00:01:23.232 --> 00:01:35.184
A twenty-nine-year-old at home reports a strong urge to push. The presenting part is visible and contractions are close together; there is no time for a long transport-first debate.
一位29岁患者在家强烈想用力，已见先露部且宫缩密集；没有时间进行冗长的先运输争论。

00:01:35.184 --> 00:01:44.232
The crew confirms scene safety, introduces its roles and asks the registered midwife what has happened and what the current plan is.
救护组确认现场安全、说明角色，并询问注册助产士已发生情况及当前计划。

00:01:44.232 --> 00:01:54.816
One clinician continues maternal ABC assessment while a second prepares a warm newborn area, timer, ventilation equipment and appropriate sizes.
一名临床人员持续母体ABC评估，另一人准备温暖新生儿区域、计时器、通气设备及适合尺寸。

00:01:54.816 --> 00:02:03.048
The training objective is controlled coordination and reassessment, not a memorized pull or an internal cervical examination.
训练目标是协调控制及复评，而不是背诵牵拉或进行内部宫颈检查。

00:02:03.048 --> 00:02:10.416
Ask about the patient’s history and the pattern of contractions while observing the presenting part and urge to push.
需询问病史及宫缩模式，同时观察先露部及用力感。

00:02:10.416 --> 00:02:16.968
The appearance of crowning or an unavoidable urge to push changes the transport and preparation decision.
出现着冠或不可避免的用力感，会改变运输及准备决定。

00:02:16.968 --> 00:02:24.432
Explain what you are doing, protect dignity and use the appropriate external support taught in the supervised birth station.
应解释正在进行的事、保护尊严，并采用监督分娩站点教授的适当外部支持。

00:02:24.432 --> 00:02:33.144
Do not perform an internal examination or use forceful traction to hurry the birth. The regional procedure and clinician roles govern.
不能进行内部检查或用力牵拉催生；应遵循区域程序及临床人员角色。

00:02:33.144 --> 00:02:40.512
Shoulder dystocia is suspected when the head delivers but the shoulders do not follow with the usual gentle sequence.
头部娩出而肩部未按通常轻柔顺序娩出时，应怀疑肩难产。

00:02:40.512 --> 00:02:49.224
Call for help promptly and follow the current L08 pathway. One person should track time and support the newborn plan.
应及时呼救并遵循现行L08路径；需有人计时并支持新生儿方案。

00:02:49.224 --> 00:02:59.448
McRoberts positioning and suprapubic pressure are distinct external maneuvers. Demonstrate them only on a training manikin under instructor supervision.
McRoberts体位与耻骨上加压是不同外部手法；仅在教师监督下用训练模型演示。

00:02:59.448 --> 00:03:09.840
Do not apply fundal pressure, forcefully pull the head or perform internal rotation, episiotomy or posterior-arm maneuvers outside the authorized role.
不得宫底加压、用力牵头，或超出授权角色进行内旋、会阴切开或后臂手法。

00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:17.664
After delivery, continue to assess the patient. Visible blood loss may understate the degree of physiological compromise.
分娩后仍需持续评估患者；可见失血量可能低估生理损害程度。

00:03:17.664 --> 00:03:29.088
Describe the patient’s perfusion, symptoms, bleeding and change over time. A soft or poorly contracted uterus can be one clue, not the whole diagnosis.
需描述灌注、症状、出血及时间变化；子宫松软或收缩差可是一条线索，但非完整诊断。

00:03:29.088 --> 00:03:38.472
The FourTs framework groups tone, trauma, tissue and thrombin. Use it to organize questions while maintaining ABC priorities.
四T框架包括张力、创伤、组织及凝血；可用来组织问题，同时维持ABC优先级。

00:03:38.472 --> 00:03:50.496
Follow current BCEHS L09 authority and consultation requirements. Do not invent a medication dose, delay support for a volume estimate or force placental delivery.
应遵循现行BCEHS L09授权及咨询要求；不能编药量、因估算血量延误支持或强行娩胎盘。

00:03:50.496 --> 00:03:56.856
Record the time of complete birth and quickly assess tone and whether breathing or crying is effective.
需记录完全出生时刻，并快速评估肌张力及呼吸哭声是否有效。

00:03:56.856 --> 00:04:04.992
Maintain warmth and use the correct local newborn sequence. A well-appearing baby still needs ongoing observation.
需维持保暖并采用正确当地新生儿顺序；外观良好仍需持续观察。

00:04:04.992 --> 00:04:14.496
If breathing is absent, gasping or ineffective after the appropriate initial steps, the central intervention is effective assisted ventilation.
适当初步处理后若无呼吸、喘息或呼吸无效，核心干预是有效辅助通气。

00:04:14.496 --> 00:04:25.008
Watch the response, especially heart-rate trend and chest movement. A minute on the clock is an urgency target, never permission to wait before indicated breaths.
需观察反应，尤其心率趋势及胸廓活动；时钟一分钟是紧迫目标，绝非等待必要通气的理由。

00:04:25.008 --> 00:04:36.624
The saved school outline and station notes say forty to sixty newborn ventilations per minute. That is the stated school objective and must remain visible for exam preparation.
学校保存的周纲及站点笔记写新生儿通气每分钟40至60次；这是明示学校目标，考试准备时须保留。

00:04:36.624 --> 00:04:48.336
The current public BCEHS M09 algorithm specifies a different range. The current service teaching is thirty to sixty breaths per minute, with rate selected within the local pathway.
当前公开BCEHS M09算法给出不同范围；现行服务教学为每分钟30至60次，并在当地路径内选频率。

00:04:48.336 --> 00:04:58.728
Do not average the ranges, call them identical or teach an invented hybrid. Effective ventilation, chest movement and heart-rate response remain central.
不能平均范围、说它们相同或编混合方案；有效通气、胸廓活动及心率反应仍是核心。

00:04:58.728 --> 00:05:10.152
Keep the dated conflict visible and confirm with the instructor what wording the assessment expects. For operational learning use the current service guideline, not an obsolete number.
需保留有日期的冲突，并向教师核实考核措辞；实际操作学习则使用现行服务指南，不用过时数字。

00:05:10.152 --> 00:05:19.920
Do not compress because the infant is apneic before effective ventilation has been attempted. Birth resuscitation prioritizes the ventilation problem.
未尝试有效通气前，不能仅因婴儿无呼吸就按压；出生复苏优先处理通气问题。

00:05:19.920 --> 00:05:28.752
Use current M09 and the selected current neonatal guidance for the persistent severe-bradycardia threshold after effective breaths.
有效呼吸后持续严重心动过缓的按压阈值，应依现行M09及选定现行新生儿指南。

00:05:28.752 --> 00:05:39.744
The saved BCPEG sheet contains an older threshold loop. It is not silently merged with the current service sequence; the course notes the discrepancy for the instructor.
保存的BCPEG表含旧阈值循环；本课不会将其静默合并进当前服务顺序，并将差异留给教师核对。

00:05:39.744 --> 00:05:53.568
When indicated, use the synchronized neonatal ratio and technique in the current local algorithm. Do not substitute the infant/child BLS sequence or copy advanced drug boxes into PCP actions.
达到条件时，应依现行当地算法使用同步新生儿比例及手法；不能替换成婴儿/儿童BLS，也不能把高级药物框复制成PCP动作。

00:05:53.568 --> 00:06:05.088
A seven-year-old had a witnessed convulsion that stopped before the crew arrived. The caregiver says the child has epilepsy but is unsure how long recovery usually takes.
一名7岁儿童的目击抽搐在救护组到达前停止；照护者称患癫痫，但不清楚平常恢复多久。

00:06:05.088 --> 00:06:17.400
The child is drowsy and breathing spontaneously. The crew assesses airway protection, ventilation, injury, temperature and the recovery trend before a detailed history.
儿童嗜睡且自主呼吸；救护组先评气道保护、通气、损伤、体温及恢复趋势，再详细问史。

00:06:17.400 --> 00:06:30.312
For this fictional practice case, bedside glucose is 2.8 mmol/L. Record the time, units, method and age; do not make the number itself a complete diagnosis.
本虚构练习中床旁血糖为2.8 mmol/L；需记录时间、单位、方法及年龄，不能把数值本身当完整诊断。

00:06:30.312 --> 00:06:42.120
Ask about baseline behavior, seizure duration, rescue plan and recent food or medicines. Continue primary assessment and seek the current pediatric pathway.
需询问基线行为、抽搐时长、救援计划及近期饮食用药；继续初评并查现行儿科路径。

00:06:42.120 --> 00:06:52.536
Appearance asks whether the child interacts in a way that fits age and baseline. A drowsy post-seizure child still needs airway and glucose attention.
外观评估儿童互动是否符合年龄及基线；抽搐后嗜睡儿童仍需关注气道及血糖。

00:06:52.536 --> 00:07:01.560
Work of breathing includes posture, effort, sounds and chest movement. Rate alone does not show whether breaths are effective.
呼吸功包括体位、用力、声音及胸廓活动；单看次数无法判断呼吸是否有效。

00:07:01.560 --> 00:07:12.576
Circulation to skin looks at colour, pallor and mottling as rapid perfusion clues. They do not replace pulse, blood pressure, temperature or a trend.
皮肤循环观察颜色、苍白及花斑，作为快速灌注线索；不能替代脉搏、血压、体温或趋势。

00:07:12.576 --> 00:07:21.144
PAT helps identify a child who needs immediate support. It does not name the cause or replace the structured primary survey.
PAT帮助识别需即时支持的儿童，但不能确定病因，也不能替代结构化初评。

00:07:21.144 --> 00:07:29.664
The saved school outline specifies a glucose threshold at or below two point six millimoles per litre for children older than one month.
学校保存周纲规定1月龄以上儿童血糖小于或等于2.6 mmol/L。

00:07:29.664 --> 00:07:39.480
The saved 7E narrative uses a broader under-four point zero statement. These are not the same threshold or necessarily the same clinical question.
保存的7E正文使用更广泛的低于4.0表述；这不是同一阈值，也不一定回答同一临床问题。

00:07:39.480 --> 00:07:50.736
Current BCEHS neonatal glucose guidance is age-specific and must not be transferred to every child. Use the appropriate current pathway for the patient’s age and condition.
现行BCEHS新生儿血糖指南有年龄特异性，不能套用所有儿童；应按患者年龄及病情查合适现行路径。

00:07:50.736 --> 00:08:03.480
For an exam, preserve the school value and ask which revision is assessed. For care, use the current service pathway. Do not erase the conflict by selecting one unlabeled number.
考试时保留学校数值并核对考核版本；实际照护用现行服务路径。不能选一个不标来源的数字来抹去冲突。

00:08:03.480 --> 00:08:12.024
Lay the child in the position and direction shown by the actual Broselow instructions; use the device’s correct head-to-heel landmarks.
应按真实Broselow说明规定的姿势及方向测量，使用正确头至脚定位点。

00:08:12.024 --> 00:08:22.488
The colour zone estimates a weight category and guides equipment selection. It is not a measured scale weight or guarantee that every child in the zone is average.
颜色区估计体重类别并提示器械尺寸；它不是实测体重，也不保证区内每名儿童都平均。

00:08:22.488 --> 00:08:33.552
Before any medication calculation, verify the actual medication, concentration, weight basis, units and maximum dose against the permitted reference.
任何药物计算前，需依据获准资料核对药品、浓度、体重依据、单位及最大剂量。

00:08:33.552 --> 00:08:42.720
The school skill is a supervised tape-estimation station. A colour band alone does not authorize a medicine or replace training and scope.
学校技能是监督下的测量尺估重站；仅凭颜色带不能授权给药，也不能替代训练及执业范围。

00:08:42.720 --> 00:08:53.616
A ten-year-old with an established tracheostomy becomes distressed after a stretcher transfer. The caregiver hands over a written airway plan and a labelled emergency kit.
一名10岁既有气切儿童在担架转运后出现窘迫；照护者交来书面气道方案及标签清晰的急救包。

00:08:53.616 --> 00:09:06.216
The team checks responsiveness, breathing, chest rise, oxygen supply and whether an attachment has kinked or disconnected. It maintains support while one member speaks with the caregiver.
团队检查反应、呼吸、胸廓起伏、氧源及附件折弯/断开，同时维持支持并由一人询问照护者。

00:09:06.216 --> 00:09:15.912
A trained station operator uses the marked catheter, but it will not pass to the patient-specific depth limit. The learner stops instead of forcing it.
受训站点操作者使用标记吸痰管，但未能达到患者个体深度；学员应停止而非强推。

00:09:15.912 --> 00:09:26.304
The team reassesses ventilation, considers obstruction or displacement, summons advanced airway help and prepares transport using the current authorized route.
团队重评通气、考虑阻塞或移位、呼叫高级气道协助，并按现行授权路径准备运输。

00:09:26.304 --> 00:09:33.816
Stop if a catheter will not pass to its measured limit, unexpected bleeding appears or the patient deteriorates.
若吸痰管无法通过测定界限、出现意外出血或患者恶化，应停止。

00:09:33.816 --> 00:09:40.800
Do not force-reinsert a displaced tube or disconnect home ventilation outside the trained local procedure.
不能强行重置移位导管，也不能超出受训当地程序断开家庭呼吸机。

00:09:40.800 --> 00:09:47.760
Continue the highest-priority respiratory support, ask for trained help and follow the current service pathway.
应继续最高优先级呼吸支持、请求受训帮助并遵循现行服务路径。

00:09:47.760 --> 00:09:56.808
Report what was directly seen and done. State which airway facts remain unknown instead of documenting a presumed diagnosis.
需报告直接观察及已做处置；应说明仍未知的气道信息，不记录推测诊断。

00:09:56.808 --> 00:10:05.976
Give the maternal and newborn teams separate clinical summaries. Do not let a single family handover obscure which findings belong to which patient.
需分别向母婴接收团队报告；不能让一次家庭交接混淆各项发现属于哪名患者。

00:10:05.976 --> 00:10:13.584
For the mother, include delivery events, bleeding and perfusion findings, response and remaining concern.
母体交接需包括分娩经过、出血灌注发现、反应及残余担忧。

00:10:13.584 --> 00:10:23.568
For the newborn, include complete-birth time, initial breathing, effective ventilation, heart-rate trend, temperature support and escalation.
新生儿交接需包括完全出生时刻、初始呼吸、有效通气、心率趋势、保温支持及升级。

00:10:23.568 --> 00:10:33.600
Identify the receiving clinician for each patient and confirm that responsibility was accepted. Continue reassessment until transfer is complete.
需明确母婴各自接收临床人员并确认责任已接收；完成交接前持续复评。

00:10:33.600 --> 00:10:40.728
Begin with what the patient’s condition did over time, rather than whether the learner remembered a preferred mnemonic.
复盘应从患者状态随时间如何变化开始，而非只看学员是否记住某口诀。

00:10:40.728 --> 00:10:48.888
Separate an unobserved skill from a knowledge statement. Saying “I know suctioning” is not evidence of safe catheter depth.
应区分未观察技能与知识陈述；会说“懂吸引”不能证明吸痰深度安全。

00:10:48.888 --> 00:10:55.920
Ask whether concerns, requests and responses were closed-loop and whether each patient had a named lead.
需问担忧、请求及反馈是否闭环，以及每名患者是否有指定负责人。

00:10:55.920 --> 00:11:03.840
Identify equipment or source conflicts without blaming a student for an inaccessible attachment or undocumented revision.
应识别器械或来源冲突；不能因学员无法获得附件或版本未记录而归咎个人。

00:11:03.840 --> 00:11:08.952
Explain the reason for the next assessment and how the finding would change your plan.
说明下一项评估的理由，以及发现会怎样改变计划。

00:11:08.952 --> 00:11:16.200
Demonstrate only the skills assigned at the station using the instructor’s equipment, current checklist and supervision.
仅用教师提供器械、现行检查表及监督演示站点指定技能。

00:11:16.200 --> 00:11:25.128
Give a concise but complete maternal, newborn, pediatric or airway report that distinguishes direct findings from caregiver history.
给出简洁完整的母体、新生儿、儿科或气道报告，并区分直接发现与照护者病史。

00:11:25.128 --> 00:11:36.912
Name the source revision and role boundary. When a school page conflicts with current service guidance, document the conflict and request clarification instead of blending instructions.
指出来源版本及角色边界；学校资料与现行服务指南冲突时，应记录并请求澄清，不拼混指令。
